    REFACTOR-0001: add the MusicSource target interface
    
    Comparing the Spotify and Apple Music loops, the SDK being called is
    the only thing that differs; what the reports do with a play is the
    same. MusicRecord is the one shape a play should have, and MusicSource
    is the one thing MyWrapped should need from a platform.
    
    We can't make SpotifyClient or AppleMusicLibrary implement MusicSource:
    they're the platforms' code, not ours.
    
    Nothing uses MusicSource yet.

diff --git a/src/MusicSource.ts b/src/MusicSource.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d2ba417
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/MusicSource.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+/** One play, in the one shape MyWrapped understands. */
+export interface MusicRecord {
+	id: string;
+	track: string;
+	artist: string;
+	streams: number;
+	genre: string;
+}
+
+/** Any platform's plays, as MusicRecords. */
+export interface MusicSource {
+	getRecords(): MusicRecord[];
+}
